VulkanLumen — Stage 1: Cornell geometry and presentation

Stage 1 is now implemented. The existing vulkan-experiment/main.cpp continues
to call the same API and does not contain any scene or shading algorithms.
Everything needed for the first visible image lives under lumen/.

Implemented:
  create()   Construct a Cornell-box mesh, vertex buffer, HDR color and D32
             depth attachments, raster pass, descriptor set and pipelines.
  record()   Rasterize visible Cornell surfaces to an offscreen color/depth
             pass, then synchronize the HDR target for subsequent reading.
  compose()  Draw a fullscreen triangle in the host presentation pass,
             sampling and tonemapping the HDR image.
  resize()   Recreate image resources and pipelines after host device idle.
  reset()    Release owned GPU resources before device shutdown.
  implemented() returns true after successful pipeline creation.

Not yet implemented:
  - Physically correct direct lighting or contact shadows (Stage 2)
  - BVH/SDF scene tracing (Stage 3)
  - Surface cards and cached material lighting (Stage 4)
  - World-space radiance cache (Stage 5)
  - Screen probe gather, screen tracing and scene-ray fallback (Stages 6–7)
  - Dynamic invalidation and multibounce (Stage 8)
  - Reflections and performance scaling (Stages 9–10)
  - External scene and G-buffer interpretation: the public setters accept
    handles, but Stage 1 draws the internal Cornell demo only.
  - result().diffuse/reflections remain null until GI passes exist.

Shaders: lumen/shaders.hpp embeds the vertex/fragment GLSL sources. The Lumen
module compiles them once when create() is called, writing temporary files
under the application's build/shaders/ directory. Install glslangValidator
and keep it in PATH. vulkan-experiment requires no shader source files.

Validation of Stage 1:
  cd vulkan-experiment
  git pull --ff-only
  rm -f c.lock
  c build run vulkan-experiment

Expected: a movable Cornell box with red and green walls, two white blocks
and a bright ceiling panel. Surfaces are intentionally UNLIT; the face
brightness differences are static preview colors, not GI. No noise or blur.
Movement: WASD + mouse. Escape closes the window.

Do not begin Stage 2 until the scene, depth occlusion and camera movement
render correctly and the baseline FPS is measured on the base M1.

Build: standalone VulkanLumen through lumen/build.c. Rendering objects rely
on VulkanGPU and VulkanRender; the application links Lumen before these
providers. Never use the removed root vulkan-systems/build.c.
